Verify Init against the problem, repository, and expert_kernel in the generation
record. Read kernel.json and submission/; require their exact files to equal
source_files. Do not edit candidate implementation or problem.

Compare the full ProblemSpec with the supplied problem and inspection records:
definition, workload, tensor order, dtype, shape, strides, and input descriptors.
{% include "backend.j4" %}
Audit the candidate against that backend's bundle contract.
Use .agents/skills/bench/SKILL.md for expert adapters and measurements.

Resolve the requested expert and fixed executable instance from the response and
staged repository. Inspect its actual instantiated definitions. Build an adapter
under expert/ that calls this original instance on the supplied stream.
Use the registered get_backend with the candidate problem's language/platform.
Construct expert with the same problem and
source_files={backend.raw_source: adapter_text}, exporting backend.raw_abi.
Pass existing repository include directories explicitly with include_paths to
klineage.harness.evaluate; the candidate remains independent of the library.

First expert_validation = evaluate(expert, workdir, include_paths=includes) against
the problem oracle; require expert_validation.accepted.
Then validation = evaluate(candidate, workdir, reference=expert, include_paths=includes).
Require validation.accepted. A supplied reference enables the harness's paired
backend timing gate: at least 0.99 baseline performance overall and in every trial.
Repeat the candidate/expert comparison independently on the frozen final sources;
require the repeated result to be accepted too.

Judge compute, tiling, pipeline synchronization, layouts, and scheduling against the
actual expert. Cite both implementations; unresolved definitions or changed
mechanisms fail. Keep source comparisons and measurement records in evaluations/.
Attach only the measured ValidationResult to kernel.json with save_kernel; preserve
all other fields. Missing measurements, unavailable tools, or failed checks mean false.

